    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "LOGICAL_OWNER = JINGO\nROLE = DIRECTING SYSTEM DESIGN\nSTATE = DESIGN PROPOSED / IMPLEMENTATION NOT STARTED\n\n## CLASSIFICATION\nARCHITECTURAL — no existing Babylon directing flow was found in Shared HQ code search, so this is a new subsystem.\n\n## JINGO DECISION\nChosen v1 scope = B.\n\nBuild only:\n- simple 3D character proxies/mannequins;\n- positions and distances;\n- readable static poses;\n- one or more cameras with explicit framing;\n- simple character motion tracks;\n- simple camera motion tracks;\n- deterministic frame/shot output for downstream SALVADOR reference use.\n\nDo NOT include in v1:\n- free-text/NLP scene generation;\n- automatic LYNCH language parsing;\n- production character meshes/body compiler dependency;\n- textures/material authoring;\n- physics-driven combat;\n- procedural animation system;\n- SALVADOR auto-submit;\n- audio/music integration;\n- canon mutation.\n\n## DESIGN LAW\n`DIRECTING INTENT -> STRUCTURED SCENE -> BABYLON BLOCKING -> CAMERA/SHOT -> FRAME`\n\nLater adapter only:\n`LYNCH TEXT -> STRUCTURED SCENE`\n\nThis keeps natural-language interpretation replaceable and prevents it from contaminating the deterministic Babylon runtime.\n\n## CORE DATA CONTRACT\nA scene document must contain:\n- scene id/version;\n- stage dimensions / ground plane;\n- actors with stable ids, proxy type/height, world transform;\n- pose definition using a minimal named joint set;\n- optional motion keyframes for actor root/joints;\n- cameras with position/target/FOV or equivalent lens framing data;\n- optional camera keyframes;\n- shot markers / frame time;\n- deterministic seed only where randomness is explicitly used.\n\n## PROXY LAW\nv1 proxies are disposable directing geometry, not Character Truth. They communicate silhouette, scale, facing, support, distance, eyeline and action geography only. No proxy measurements may write back into locked character canon.\n\n## CAMERA LAW\nCamera interprets action; it does not auto-follow it. Every camera motion has explicit start, target, duration and settle. No automatic shake.\n\n## MOTION LAW\nv1 motion is blocking-level only: translate/turn/raise/step/lean/simple limb keyframes. It proves timing and geography, not final animation quality.\n\n## OUTPUT\nThe first accepted proof should show one small scene with 2 proxies, deliberate spacing, distinct poses, one fixed shot plus one simple camera or actor move, and reproducible frame capture suitable as a SALVADOR reference.\n\n## ACCEPTANCE\nPASS requires:\n1. same scene JSON produces the same blocking and camera framing;\n2. actor ids/transforms/poses are inspectable;\n3. simple motion can be scrubbed/replayed deterministically;\n4. camera framing is explicit and stable;\n5. still frame can be exported/captured for SALVADOR;\n6. no dependency on textures, production character meshes, NLP, paid services or external inference;\n7. no canon writeback;\n8. independent DUNCAN QC before any production integration.\n\n## NEXT GATE\nImplementation MUST NOT start until OWNER accepts this design. After acceptance: write formal spec -> implementation plan -> LESTER TDD implementation -> DUNCAN QC.\n\nOWNER APPROVAL PHRASE:\n`APPROVE BABYLON DIRECTING V1 DESIGN`",
